\name{cellucid_analysis_window_place}
\alias{cellucid_analysis_window_place}
\title{Move or resize an analysis window}
\usage{
cellucid_analysis_window_place(viewer, window, left, top, width, height)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{window}{A floating analysis window, by its number (1 is the first open). A whole number (at least 1). Required.}
\item{left}{A number. Required.}
\item{top}{A number. Required.}
\item{width}{A number (more than 0). Required.}
\item{height}{A number (more than 0). Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Give a floating analysis window a place and size; it is kept inside the window.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{analysis.window.place} (Analysis). It changes the viewer's layout: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{layout}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_analysis_window_place(viewer, height = 1,
      left = 0, top = 0, width = 1, window = 1)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
